The translated program uses exactly the expected constructors, including an initial docstring expression and a deeply nested `If` chain. I’m representing GPAs as exact rationals `num(P,Q)` in the runtime semantics, so proof obligations use linear integer arithmetic and avoid unsound assumptions about decimal rounding; each Python float threshold is translated once to its exact decimal rational.
